From 12943d73c8f840e1afce9177c1935e72a13f1a49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 04:26:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02259/11362] [outer-loop] (a) multi-round refactor loop + (c)
 verifier-routed cascade in choose_action

(a) arc_e3_agent_solve.py: induce then REFACTOR up to N rounds (feed mismatches back),
keep the BEST engine seen, record accuracy_history -- the cheap accuracy lever to lift the
27% cd82 model toward solvable. Also --repo for the open-model benchmark (b).
(c) E3AgentPolicy is now the VERIFIER-ROUTED CASCADE: tier-1 explorer; escalate to tier-3
E3 induction ONLY on STALL (budget spent w/o a level-up, or explored-out) and only ONCE,
then tier-1 fallback. make_carnot_agent(cascade=True) uses it by default (the competition
path). Validated offline: escalates exactly once (explore->induce->explore), replay path
intact 11/11. The Meta-EBM-Cascade-Router made concrete: cheap-first, escalate the hard tail.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 python/carnot/agentic/arc_competition_agent.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/python/carnot/agentic/arc_competition_agent.py b/python/carnot/agentic/arc_competition_agent.py
index 9fb06f7e46..8b24674929 100644
--- a/python/carnot/agentic/arc_competition_agent.py
+++ b/python/carnot/agentic/arc_competition_agent.py
@@ -313,7 +313,7 @@ class E3AgentPolicy:
             # first, escalate the hard tail.
             won = self.explorer.best_level > (self.explorer.start_level or 0)
             stalled = len(self.transitions) >= self.explore_budget or self.explorer.explored_out
-            if stalled and not won:
+            if stalled and not won and not self.induced:   # escalate ONCE; then tier-1 fallback
                 self.phase = "induce"
             return mv
         if self.phase == "induce" and not self.induced:
